<section class="rail opening">
    <div class="opening-grid">
        <div>
            <p class="status" data-reveal style="--i:0">
                <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                Open to work
            </p>

            <h1 data-reveal style="--i:1">
                I build software that has to hold up <em>after</em> the demo.
            </h1>

            <p class="lede" data-reveal style="--i:2">
                I'm Lewis — a developer in Nairobi. Websites, APIs, a little machine
                learning, the odd Android app. Most of what I've made was for someone
                specific, and I can tell you what I'd change about all of it.
            </p>

            <div class="actions" data-reveal style="--i:3">
                <a class="btn" href="/work">See the work</a>
                <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="portrait" data-reveal style="--i:2">
            <img src="/images/profile.jpg" alt="Lewis Mucheru, smiling, in a dark suit and navy tie" width="640" height="800">
            <figcaption>That's me.<br>Nairobi, most days.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="rail band" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="eyebrow" id="work-heading">Selected work</h2>
        <p>Three I'd sit down and walk you through</p>
    </div>

    <div class="index">
        {{#each projects}}
        {{> index-item project=this index=@index}}
        {{/each}}
    </div>

    <p class="form-note" data-reveal style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <a class="link" href="/work">All six projects</a>
    </p>
</section>

<section class="measure band" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <h2 class="eyebrow" id="how-heading" data-reveal>How I work</h2>
    <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--i:1">
        <p>
            I finished a BSc in Software Development at KCA University in 2025 and
            learned the stack the long way round — databases, then interfaces, then
            APIs, then the machine-learning parts that only earn a place if they
            help somebody.
        </p>
        <p>
            The through-line in everything below is the same: I'd rather build the
            unglamorous half properly than the demo-able half quickly. Admin
            screens, error states, the thing that happens on a bad connection. That
            is usually where the product actually lives.
        </p>
        <p>
            <a class="link" href="/about">More about me</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="measure band--tight" style="padding-bottom:clamp(4rem,10vw,7rem)">
    <div data-reveal>
        <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Looking for someone?</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:1.75rem">
            I'm open to work and I read every note that comes in — roles,
            collaborations, or "I just liked the site."
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn" href="/contact">Say hello</a>
            <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/files/Lewis-Mucheru-Resume.pdf" download>Download résumé</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
